&lt;h1&gt;


  Automating Multi‑Platform Article Publishing with a Node.js Content Pipeline
&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; I built a tiny Node.js pipeline that pulls a single source markdown, injects front‑matter, writes platform‑specific files, and flips flags in &lt;code&gt;metadata.json&lt;/code&gt;. The result is a reproducible, zero‑touch publish step that keeps Medium, Substack, and Dev.to in sync.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  The Problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every week I write a single article in a &lt;code&gt;src/&lt;/code&gt; folder, then manually copy‑paste it into three different publishing platforms (Medium, Substack, Dev.to). The process was fragile:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Missed line breaks caused malformed HTML on Medium.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substack rejected the file because the front‑matter was missing.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dev.to’s API returned &lt;code&gt;422 Unprocessable Entity&lt;/code&gt; when the article body contained stray carriage returns (&lt;code&gt;\r&lt;/code&gt;).
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The symptom was a cascade of alerts in ClickUp: “Medium draft not generated”, “Substack draft missing”, “Dev.to build failed”. I needed a reliable way to generate the three platform‑specific markdown files from a single source and keep a JSON manifest up‑to‑date.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What I Tried First
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;My first attempt was a Bash one‑liner that used &lt;code&gt;sed&lt;/code&gt; to replace placeholders:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;sed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"s/{{date}}/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;date&lt;/span&gt; +%F&lt;span class="si"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/"&lt;/span&gt; src/article.md &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; content/2026/10/04/content-automation/medium_en.md
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;It worked for the date placeholder, but quickly fell apart:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Path brittleness:&lt;/strong&gt; Hard‑coded dates (&lt;code&gt;2026/10/04&lt;/code&gt;) meant the script broke on the next day.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Encoding issues:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;sed&lt;/code&gt; left Windows line endings (&lt;code&gt;\r\n&lt;/code&gt;) in the output, causing Dev.to’s API to reject the payload.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No state tracking:&lt;/strong&gt; I had no way to know which platforms had already been generated, leading to duplicate PRs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Because the script was not extensible, I abandoned it and started building a proper Node.js tool.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The Implementation
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Project layout
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;content-automation/
├─ src/
│  └─ article.md                # single source (raw markdown)
├─ scripts/
│  └─ generate.js               # pipeline entry point
├─ content/
│  └─ 2026/10/04/content-automation/
│     ├─ medium_en.md
│     ├─ medium_es.md
│     ├─ substack_en.md
│     ├─ substack_es.md
│     └─ metadata.json
└─ package.json
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  &lt;code&gt;metadata.json&lt;/code&gt; – the source of truth
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before the change &lt;code&gt;metadata.json&lt;/code&gt; looked like this (excerpt from the diff):&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight diff"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="gd"&gt;-  "medium_generated": false,
-  "substack_generated": false,
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="gi"&gt;+  "medium_generated": true,
+  "substack_generated":
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;I expanded it to a full manifest that tracks each platform:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"repo"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"content-automation"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"date"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"2026-10-04"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"languages"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"es"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"en"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"topics"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Productivity"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"commits"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"pull_requests"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"releases"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"closed_issues"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"generated"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"medium_en"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"medium_es"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"substack_en"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"substack_es"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The pipeline updates these flags after a successful write, so the next run knows what’s already been produced.&lt;/p&gt;

